.TH MKGRD 1ggl "11 Dec 2000" "GGL/IGP ETHZ" "GGL Common Lib"
.SH NAME
mkgrd \- Gridding an ASCII file to grd or surfer file format
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmkgrd\fP \fIxyzfile\fP \fB\-G\fP\fIgrdfile\fP \fB\-I\fP\fIx_inc\fP[/\fIy_inc\fP]
\fB\-R\fP\fIwest/east/south/north\fP [ \fB\-b\fP\fIx_blocks\fP[/\fIy_blocks\fP] ] [ \fB\-D\fP ]
[ \fB\-e\fP\fIepsilon\fP ]  [ \fB\-f\fP\fIpointfile\fP ] [ \fB\-h\fP ] [ \fB\-M\fP[\fIminimum\fP] ] [ \fB\-n\fP\fIexponent\fP ]
[ \fB\-Q\fP ] [ \fB\-q\fP ] [ \fB\-r\fP\fIradius\fP ] [ \fB\-s\fP ] [ \fB\-S\fP ] [ \fB\-V\fP ] [ \fB\-z\fP ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmkgrd\fP reads a xyz table of arbitrary distributed points and
creates a binary grdfile.  \fBmkgrd\fP will report if some of 
the nodes are not filled in with
data.  Such unconstrained nodes are set to NaN.
.TP
\fIxyzfile\fP
ASCII file holding (x,y,z) values.  The triplets do not
have to be sorted. Lines beginning with `#' are treated
as comment lines.
.TP
.B \-G
\fIgrdfile\fP is the name of the binary (or ASCII, see \fB\-s\fP)
output grdfile.
.TP
.B \-I
\fIx_inc\fP [and optionally \fIy_inc\fP] is the grid spacing.
Not needed if \fB\-f\fP is supplied.
.TP
.B \-R
\fIwest, east, south,\fP and \fInorth\fP specify the region of interest.
.SH OPTIONS
.sp
.TP
.B \-b
\fIx_blocks\fP [and optionally \fIy_blocks\fP] is the number of blocks
\fBmkgrd\fP will use for processing within the \fB\-R\fP boundaries.
By default, this value is calculated from region boundaries and radius.
.TP
.B \-D
This option is used only in conjunction with \fB\-f\fP. It causes
\fBmkgrd\fP to print input point height and difference between
input point height and interpolated point height.
.TP
.B \-e
\fIepsilon\fP is the smoothing factor in the weight function 
w= \fIepsilon\fP^n /( d^n + \fIepsilon\fP^n ), where d stands for
the distance between output grid point and input point. The exponent
\fIn\fP is chosen by the option \fB\-n\fP. [ Default is 
\fIepsilon\fP = 1e-5 ].
.TP
.B \-f
\fIpointfile\fP is used to acquire the \fIx\fP and \fIy\fP coordinates of
the target interpolation point instead of a regular grid.
Using this option changes the meaning of several other options.
Points outside \fB\-R\fP will be ignored. Option \fB\-I\fP
is meaningless and thus not required anymore. The file supplied 
by \fB\-G\fP will not be a grid file, but an ASCII output file
containing \fIx\fP, \fIy\fP and interpolated \fIh\fP.
If \fB\-D\fP is supplied, input \fIh\fP and the height difference 
will be written as fourth and fifth column as well.
.TP
.B \-h
Given this option, \fBmkgrd\fP gives a short help information and
exits immediately, ignoring all other parameters passed to it.
.TP
.B \-M
The quadrant method of checking, if we are interpolating and not
extrapolating is turned off. (See also option \fB\-Q\fP)
\fIminimum\fP determines
how many points must at least be allocated to a grid point in
order to be a valid interpolation. This option implies \fB\-Q\fP.
.TP
.B \-n
The exponent in the weight function. (See option \fB\-e\fP)
[ Default is 2 ]
.TP
.B \-Q
The quadrant method of checking, if we are interpolating and not
extrapolating is turned off. This is the same as giving option
\fB\-M\fP1. By default, a grid point will only be interpolated, when
all 4 quadrants around a grid point contain at least one point
contributing to the interpolation.
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet operation. If not set, \fBmkgrd\fP will send progress reports to stderr.
.TP
.B \-r
All points within \fIradius\fP contribute to a grid point interpolation.
[Default: 20.0 m] (See also \fB\-e\fP)
.TP
.B \-s
Output grid is ASCII surfer grid format [Default is GMT binary grid].
.TP
.B \-S
Output grid as ASCII stream: x y z format [Default is GMT binary grid].
.TP
.B \-V
Show version information and exit immediately.
.TP
.B \-z
This option is used only in conjunction with \fB\-f\fP. When it is
set, a point with r<0.1 get assigned a weight zero. This is used to
exclude the point to be interpolated from the domain contributing
to the interpolated height.
.SH EXAMPLES
To create a grdfile from the ASCII data in aaregletscher.xyz, try
.br
.sp
mkgrd aaregletscher.xyz \fB\-r\fP10.0 \fB\-e\fP1.0
\fB\-G\fPaare99.grd \fB\-R\fP653300/653400/161200/161300 \fB\-I\fP5\fB \-q\fP
.br
.sp
.SH SEE ALSO
gmt, xyz2grd, grd2xyz, grdedit, grdinfo
